# The build context is the repository root, so that a runner image can COPY the
# shared harness (`backend/app/services/_runner_harness.py`). That is the whole
# reason the context is the root rather than `docker/`.
#
# These exclusions keep the context small. `frontend/node_modules` alone is
# about 7,500 files, and it would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every
# single build.
#
# Deliberately *not* using a bare `*` with `!` re-includes: Docker cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so that idiom needs a
# verbose re-include of every directory on the path and breaks quietly when it
# is got wrong.

frontend/
dist/
node_modules/

backend/.venv/
backend/alembic/versions/__pycache__/

.git/
.github/

**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

design.md
tokens.css
plan.md
